    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "PAN AMERICAN WORLD AIRWAYS\n135 EAST 42nd ST. NEW YORK 17, N. Y.\nPAA-LOAD EVENT\nFIRST FLIGHT\n18th NATIONAL AMA\nMODEL AIRPLANE MEET\nJuly 31, 1949\nOlathe, Kansas\nAIR MAIL\nJUL\n31\n6 P,M\n5-9\nVia Air Mail\nMr. Harold M. Bixby\n27 East 62nd Street\nNew York 21, N. Y.\nU.S.POSTAGE",
      "THIS IS YOUR PAA-LOAD EVENT\nFIRST FLIGHT COVER\nYour PAA-Load Event First flight cover was flown\nin a model airplane which participated in the 18th\nNational AMA Model Airplane Meet, and was air\nmailed to you from the post office at Olathe, Kansas.\nThe PAA-Load Event, sponsored by Pan American\nWorld Airways, is for free flight gas models in the\nR.O.G. (rise off ground) category. The model is re-\nquired to carry a pay load consisting of eight ounces\nfor Class A, and 16\nounces\nfor the larger Class B\nmodels. For the special model mail flight the pay load\nconsisted of bundles of first flight covers.\nThe gas model Nationals were held this year at\nthe U. S. Naval Air Station Olathe. Sponsors were\nthe Olathe Chamber of Commerce and American Legion\nPost 153. The contest carried the sanction of the\nAcademy of Model Aeronautics."
    ],
